# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values.
# .env.local is gitignored — secrets must NEVER be committed.
#
# These are NOT needed for the current read-only v1. They become relevant once
# we add dynamic features (e.g. event registration, live schedule, saved favorites).

# --- Supabase (public, browser-safe) ---
# Anything prefixed with VITE_ is bundled into the browser. Only put PUBLIC keys here.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Server-only secrets (do NOT put these here) ---
# The Supabase service_role key and database password are admin credentials.
# Never expose them to the browser. Store them in Netlify's environment-variable
# settings (Site settings -> Environment variables) for any server/build use only.

# --- Petfinder (server-only — set these in Netlify, NOT here) ---
# Powers the live adoptable-rabbits list on the Adopt page via the Netlify
# function at netlify/functions/petfinder.js. These are NOT VITE_-prefixed on
# purpose: they must stay server-side and never reach the browser. Until they're
# set, the app shows its built-in sample rabbits.
#   1. Register a (free) app at https://www.petfinder.com/developers/
#   2. Add these in Netlify -> Site settings -> Environment variables:
#        PETFINDER_CLIENT_ID
#        PETFINDER_CLIENT_SECRET
#        PETFINDER_ORG_ID        <- OHRR's Petfinder organization id (e.g. OH123)
